body:
- **no children**: just remove it (the parent gets an empty child);
- **one child**: the child takes its place (the parent links straight to the child);
- **two children**: the hole cannot be filled by one child, so take the **in-order successor**, the smallest value of the right subtree, copy its value into the node, and then delete the successor from the right subtree. The successor has no left child, so that delete is one of the easy cases.

